---
title: Fudgy Vegan Brownies
portions: 16
category: Dessert
source: "https://www.lovingitvegan.com/vegan-brownies/"
---

## Batter

[Soak] Whisk the @flaxseed{25 g} with the @water{120 ml}(hot) in a #bowl{} and leave to thicken while you prepare the rest, ~{10 min}.

[Preheat] Preheat the #oven{} to ^{177°C}. Line a 9×9 square #baking dish{} with parchment paper.

[Combine] Sift the @flour{180 g} and the @cocoa{100 g} into a #mixing bowl{}. Add the @baking-powder{4 g} and the @salt{3 g} and mix.

[Melt] Add the @vegan-butter{170 g} and the @chocolate-chips{70 g} to a microwave-safe #bowl{}. Microwave in 30-second intervals, stirring between each, until melted.

[Mix] Whisk the @sugar{400 g}, the @vanilla-extract{10 ml} and the soaked flaxseed into the melted chocolate.

[Fold] Pour the wet mixture over the dry ingredients and mix into a thick batter. Fold in the remaining @chocolate-chips{70 g}.

## Bake

[Bake] Transfer to the prepared #baking dish{} and smooth down. Press a few extra @chocolate-chips{} on top. Bake until dry and shiny on top and a toothpick comes out with moist crumbs, ~{40 min}.

[Cool] Cool in the #pan{}, ~{15 min}, then lift out with the parchment overhang and cool completely before slicing.
